{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 36, :comments ["<b>It is a solemn assembly</b> — 'I detain you before Me,' like a king who invited his sons to a banquet for so many days; when the time came to let them go, he said: I ask of you, stay with me one more day, for your departure is difficult for me — this is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Leviticus 23:36). And this aggadah is found in Vayikra Rabbah.\n\nAnd by way of truth: for six days did YHWH make the heavens and the earth (Exodus 20:11), and the seventh day is Sabbath and has no pair, and Kenesset Yisrael is his pair, as it says, 'and the earth,' and behold it is the eighth — 'it is a solemn assembly' — for there all is held back. And He commanded in the Festival of Matzot seven days in holiness before them and after them, for all of them are holy and the Divine Presence is among them, and from it He counted forty-nine days — seven weeks, as the days of old — and He sanctified the eighth day like the eighth of the Festival, and the days counted in between are like the intermediate days of the Festival between the first and the eighth, and it is the day of the giving of the Torah, in which He showed them the great fire and they heard His words from within the fire. And therefore our Rabbies of blessed memory call the Festival of Weeks everywhere 'Atzeret,' for it is like the eighth day of the Festival, which Scripture so called.\n\nAnd this is their statement (Hagigah 17a): 'The eighth day is a festival unto itself with regard to PZR KShB' (the laws of festival offerings and the like), 'yet it is a supplement to the first,' for it is the emanation of the first ones and is not part of their unity. And therefore in the section of all the firstborn (Deuteronomy 16:15), He mentions the three pilgrimage festivals — the Festival of Matzot, the Festival of Weeks, and the Festival of Sukkot seven days — but does not mention the eighth, for there it says 'every male among you shall appear,' and so on. And behold, this is explained."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {0 "In the kabbalistic passage, I have rendered בת זוג as 'pair' following Ramban's usage in the sense of a counterpart or consort; the term carries technical sefirotic resonance that is left cryptic per his convention."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:58:46.467846392Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}